From 2390b438381cee3af7c85ab27456cb6f6ef08c22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeltaTor <deltator@example.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 04:23:01 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 39/40] conflux: add ConfluxSetSelection 5, give every stream
 to the fastest set

ConfluxSetSelection already has a mode (4) that spreads new streams in
proportion to each set's measured download throughput, with a 10% floor so no
set is starved. Add mode 5, which uses the same measurement but is pure
exploit: every new stream goes to the set with the highest measured throughput,
with no floor and no weighted spread.

The consequence is deliberate: the current leader keeps all new streams until
its estimate decays to zero, at which point the whole pool is back at 0 B/s and
mode 5 falls back to spreading new streams uniformly at random so every set is
sampled again and a new fastest set can be found. That fallback also covers the
first seconds after startup, before anything has been measured. Mode 5 keeps
bypassing the ConfluxSetRttMax/ConfluxSetRttPct filters, as mode 4 does, so all
sets remain measurable.

The ConfluxProbeLog diagnostics follow both modes: the candidate-table printing
moves into a shared helper, exploit picks get their own pick line, and the
periodic level-3 summary drops the floor/total-weight fields in exploit mode.
